<topic id="git-addon-open-project-gitignore">
    <title>Open ignore files</title>
    <body>
    <p>Git has two kinds of ignore files: <codeph>.gitignore</codeph> and global
        <codeph>ignore</codeph>. Use the .gitignore file to exclude files from repository or
      project-level version control, and the global <codeph>ignore</codeph> file to exclude files
      from version control across all repositories on a your machine. </p>
    <p>To open ignore files, go to <uicontrol
        conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/gs0-git-staging-view"/>
      <b>></b>
      <uicontrol conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/gs1-unstaged-files"/> and
      right-click a file or folder to open the contextual menu.</p>
    <ul id="ul_aw5_s1y_jjc">
      <li>To open a project's <codeph>.gitignore</codeph>, select <uicontrol
          conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/ignore"/>
        <b>></b>
        <uicontrol conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/open-gitignore"/>.</li>
      <li>To open the global <codeph>ignore</codeph> file, select <uicontrol
          conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/ignore"/>
        <b>></b>
        <uicontrol conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/open-ignore"/>. </li>
    </ul>
    </body>
</topic>
